{"id":"8C","title":"Judges & Magistrates","part":{"n":8,"title":"Government & civil officers"},"url":"/law/08-government-civil-officers/8c","entries":[{"id":"8C.1","text":"Judges were originally established by God.","refs":[{"book":"Judges","chapter":2,"verses":"16,18"},{"book":"2 Samuel","chapter":7,"verses":"11"}],"citation":"Judges 2:16, 18; 2 Sam. 7:11."},{"id":"8C.2","text":"Judges shall justify the righteous and condemn the wicked.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":25,"verses":"1-3"}],"citation":"Deut. 25:1-3."},{"id":"8C.3","text":"Judges shall righteously judge the causes and transgressions between persons with just judgment.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":19,"verses":"15"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":1,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":16,"verses":"18"},{"book":"1 Samuel","chapter":2,"verses":"25"},{"book":"2 Samuel","chapter":7,"verses":"11"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":19,"verses":"5"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":82,"verses":"2-4"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":31,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"Lev. 19:15; Deut 1: 16; Deut 16:18; 1 Sam. 2:25; 2 Sam. 7:11; 2 Chron. 19:5; Psa. 82:2-4; Prov. 31:9."},{"id":"8C.4","text":"Judges are not to be partial or respect persons in judgment, but shall equally judge the small as well as the great.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":23,"verses":"31"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":1,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":19,"verses":"15"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":19,"verses":"7"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":18,"verses":"5"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":24,"verses":"23"},{"book":"James","chapter":2,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"Exod. 23:31 6; Deut 1:17; Lev. 19:15; 2 Chron. 19:7; Prov. 18:5; Prov. 24:23; James 2:9."},{"id":"8C.5","text":"Judges are not to take a gift or bribe.","refs":[{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":19,"verses":"7"}],"citation":"2 Chron. 19:7."},{"id":"8C.6","text":"Judges are to judge the people at all times.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":18,"verses":"22,26"}],"citation":"Exod. 18:22, 26."},{"id":"8C.7","text":"Judges and magistrates are to know the laws of God.","refs":[{"book":"Ezra","chapter":7,"verses":"25"}],"citation":"Ezra 7:25."},{"id":"8C.8","text":"Judges judge not for man but for God.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":1,"verses":"17"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":19,"verses":"6"}],"citation":"Deut. 1: 17; 2 Chron. 19:6."},{"id":"8C.9","text":"The judge that justifies the wicked and condemns the just is an abomination to God.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":17,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"Prov. 17:15."},{"id":"8C.10","text":"Wisdom and knowledge is needed and should be prayed for in order to judge between good and bad.","refs":[{"book":"1 Kings","chapter":3,"verses":"9"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":1,"verses":"10"},{"book":"James","chapter":1,"verses":"5"}],"citation":"1 Kings 3:9; 2 Chron. 1:10; James 1:5."},{"id":"8C.11","text":"Judges are to judge matters according to the laws, statutes, commandments, and judgments of God.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":18,"verses":"16"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":19,"verses":"10"}],"citation":"Exod. 18:16; 2 Chron. 19:10."}]}